BOUNDARY SPREAD across the 5 positions (max/min of the first budget reaching a depth):
   min 1.00, median 2.00, max 3.00  (1.00 = perfectly stable across positions)
ADVICE: READ THE STAIRCASE PER POSITION. The boundaries move by up to 3.00x across real
positions, so a single fixed N is not safe; the per-position bands above are the tool.

WITHIN a position the total is constant inside a band (that is what makes the staircase), and
the ratio total/N therefore depends only on where N falls inside the band - so a budget should
be placed at or just above a band's FIRST budget, not at its last.
